# Review: ClaudePlugin

Both halves of the plugin are built. The managed-agent half has the two types, seven operations, the API client and
the skill; its pure parts (config projection, transcript filtering, the retry predicate, `listEvents` ordering,
foreign keys, credential-name validation) are unit-tested, but no test runs an operation handler, so create, deploy,
session, vault and credential behaviour is untested. The Claude Code half (ACP agent, worktrees, Composer MCP, MCP
proxying, the EDGE agent and its credential lending) is covered well by unit tests and by gated e2e suites.

Two divergences matter. The spec's "Set" and "Revoke" credential operations are one `UpdateSessionCredentials`
operation (with `refresh`), so the skill has seven tools, not eight (F-5.1). And `isRetryable` retries 403 on both
GET and POST, which F-6.4 and F-6.5 forbid; the code comments justify it as the edge proxy's transient 403.

Of 46 items: 14 done, 24 untested, 4 partial, 3 diverged, 1 missing. The QA tests are judged as automation: QA-1
(blocked, manual) has none; QA-2 to QA-5 are partly exercised by the gated e2e suites, with the UI steps walked only by
autocue flows.

